@* HelpNotificationsPage: help topic "E-mail notifications" at "/help/email-notifications". Static text only: what an
   e-mail tells you, what is never in one, how to confirm your address with a code, the three choices of when to get
   e-mail, and how to stop it. It says that the feature is there only when the administrator has set up mail. *@
@page "/help/email-notifications"

<HelpTopicFrame Slug="email-notifications">
    <section class="card">
        <p><strong>E-mail notifications</strong> can tell you by e-mail that something is waiting for you, so you do not
            have to keep the inbox open. They are optional, they are off until you turn them on, and they are there only
            when the administrator has set up mail for this server.</p>
        <h2>What you get</h2>
        <p>An e-mail says that there is news. It names the kind of news (for example a review to answer or to sign),
            the project and the review, and it has a link that opens the review. The link asks you to sign in, as
            always. The subject line never names a review. The e-mail is only a nudge: your inbox stays the complete
            list of what is waiting for you.</p>
        <h2>What is never in an e-mail</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>No comments and no answers.</li>
            <li>No verdicts and no outcomes of a review.</li>
            <li>No contents of any file.</li>
            <li>No password. The only code you ever get by e-mail is the confirmation code described below.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Confirm your address</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Open the <strong>Account</strong> page and find the <strong>E-mail notifications</strong> card.</li>
            <li>Type your e-mail address and press <strong>Send confirmation code</strong>.</li>
            <li>We send a message with a 6-digit code to that address. The code works for 30 minutes.</li>
            <li>Type the code into the card, while you are signed in, and press <strong>Confirm address</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If you ask for a new code, only the newest one works. Nothing is sent to an address until you have
            confirmed it. Your address is shown only on your own Account page.</p>
        <h2>Choose when</h2>
        <p>After you have confirmed an address, choose one of three settings in the card and press <strong>Save</strong>:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>No e-mail</strong>: nothing is sent. This is the setting you start with.</li>
            <li><strong>Daily summary</strong>: at most one e-mail a day with what is new for you.</li>
            <li><strong>Every change</strong>: an e-mail a few minutes after something new needs your attention.
                Several changes that come close together are collected into one e-mail.</li>
        </ul>
        <h2>Stop it</h2>
        <p>Choose <strong>No e-mail</strong> and press <strong>Save</strong>, or press
            <strong>Remove my address</strong> to have the address forgotten. Every e-mail with news ends with a link to your
            <strong>Account</strong> page, where you can do either.</p>
        <h2>If the card says it is not set up</h2>
        <p>Then the administrator has not switched on e-mail for this server. There is nothing you can do on the
            Account page; ask the person who runs the server. Your inbox works in the same way as always.</p>
        <p class="muted">Confirming an address, choosing a setting and removing the address are recorded in the audit
            trail, never the address or the code.</p>
    </section>
</HelpTopicFrame>
